  "id": "COMPOUND:231 - PROTEIN:429",
  "verbalization": "Butalbital is linked to Matrix metalloproteinase-9 through a series of target relationships, with the gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit alpha-6 and alpha-4 serving as intermediate targets. These subunits are both targets of different compounds, with Butalbital directly targeting alpha-6 and alpha-4, and the latter being targeted by quinidine barbiturate. The presence of Matrix metalloproteinase-9 as a target in both pathways suggests a potential role in the biological processes regulated by these receptor subunits. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where Butalbital may influence the activity of Matrix metalloproteinase-9 through the activation of gamma-aminobutyric acid receptors, potentially modulating extracellular matrix remodeling or other physiological processes. The evidence supports a functional link between Butalbital and Matrix metalloproteinase-9, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
